            <ArticleTitle>Techniques for efficient, real-time, 3D visualization of multi-modality cardiac data using consumer graphics hardware.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>463-75</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We exploit consumer graphics hardware to perform real-time processing and visualization of high-resolution, 4D cardiac data. We have implemented real-time, realistic volume rendering, interactive 4D motion segmentation of cardiac data, visualization of multi-modality cardiac data and 3D display of multiple series cardiac MRI. We show that an ATI Radeon 9700 Pro can render a 512x512x128 cardiac Computed Tomography (CT) study at 0.9 to 60 frames per second (fps) depending on rendering parameters and that 4D motion based segmentation can be performed in real-time. We conclude that real-time rendering and processing of cardiac data can be implemented on consumer graphics cards.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
